<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>BBC News</title><subtitle type="html">BBC News - Technology</subtitle><id>https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:26:05Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss.xml" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/technology" /><link rel="via" href="https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Binance says fake job interviews used as part of $6.3bn crypto hack</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ck5ynwz9gy67o#0</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:26:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T16:19:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ck5ynwz9gy67o--6b6c7100781c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ck5ynwz9gy67o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">An engineer was contacted through a legitimate job-hunting platform and invited to bogus job interviews with fake company representatives, Binance says.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK meat industry hit by cyber-attack which targeted European supermarket freezers</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckq6ndq8l6v0o#0</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:24:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T13:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckq6ndq8l6v0o--a4648347bec4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckq6ndq8l6v0o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Supermarkets in countries including Ireland, Sweden  and Belgium reported fridges being hiked in temperature on Monday.</summary></entry><entry><title>Apple unsure when it will get more foldable iPhones ahead of Christmas</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6n8dn457ypko#0</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T11:10:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6n8dn457ypko--9da12d45db34.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6n8dn457ypko?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The tech giant reports strong sales but admits "constraints" are affecting supplies of the iPhone Duo.</summary></entry><entry><title>North Korea denies being behind record $6.3bn Binance hack</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6rey4v53exgo#0</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T08:33:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6rey4v53exgo--860a0e7c55ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6rey4v53exgo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">US government agencies and cyber analysts have blamed Pyongyang for the record-breaking heist.</summary></entry><entry><title>If hackers can take control of a supermarket freezer, how vulnerable is other tech?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckpqg8lve73go#0</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T18:25:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckpqg8lve73go--5b9f2f37879a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ckpqg8lve73go?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Dozens of shops across European countries have been hit by a cyber-attack affecting their fridges.</summary></entry><entry><title>Binance users withdraw $3.6bn after largest-ever crypto hack</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwj34gdmnly4o#0</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T07:42:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwj34gdmnly4o--62fdb0afd878.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cwj34gdmnly4o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The exchange froze transactions following the incident which has been linked to a North Korean group.</summary></entry><entry><title>These firms you've never heard of are feeding fears the AI bubble could burst</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cje36degrgv5o#0</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:04Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T01:37:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cje36degrgv5o--de7377484e8d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cje36degrgv5o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The amount of debt held by data centres is measured in the tens of billions of pounds.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why North Korea's 'elite' hackers are the prime suspect in major Binance hack</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ck9dz3v7z7v3o#0</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T02:12:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ck9dz3v7z7v3o--d13e42607d01.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ck9dz3v7z7v3o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">If the accusations are true, the record-making heist shows how powerful suspected North Korean hackers have become.</summary></entry><entry><title>US tech stocks see sharp falls as AI spending nears $1tn</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cvwy72e0n72yo#0</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T20:34:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cvwy72e0n72yo--0de680b82ffb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cvwy72e0n72yo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Shares in Intel continue to fall while the tech-heavy Nasdaq opens at its lowest level in more than two months.</summary></entry><entry><title>Google value plunges by $500bn as its own AI search hits ad sales</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm9qzdqpxy48o#0</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T12:04:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm9qzdqpxy48o--2fa2c9ea3336.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm9qzdqpxy48o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Google spooked investors so badly that its stock hit a six-month low, after it revealed its AI own search summaries were affecting ad revenue.</summary></entry><entry><title>Who could be behind the Binance hack and what we know so far</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm5yn8eqg3npo#0</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T11:57:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm5yn8eqg3npo--b051c885d738.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm5yn8eqg3npo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Binance has been hit by what could be the biggest crypto hack ever - here's what we know so far</summary></entry><entry><title>From Bitcoin to Binance: Crypto terms and what they mean</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cy5w2k5k5ylo#0</id><updated>2026-11-03T16:23:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T11:35:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cy5w2k5k5ylo--8f29bac19c4b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cy5w2k5k5ylo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The Binance hack has thrust cryptocurrencies back into headlines - but what are they and how do they work?</summary></entry><entry><title>Crypto giant Binance hit by $6.3bn hack suspected to be largest in history</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk